<LearnLayout
  title="Groups: Short Tasks Inside a Project — Learn — cntxt"
  description="How a Group nests under a Project, swaps its tabs in and out, and auto-advances when completed."
  path="/learn/groups"
>
  <a href="/learn" class="back-link">← Learn</a>
  <h1>Groups: short tasks inside a Project</h1>
  <p>
    A Group is a short-lived sub-task. It can live standalone — its own
    window, same as a Project — or nest under a Project. Nested, activating
    it swaps its own tabs into that Project's already-open window in place
    of what was there. Completing a Group closes those tabs (without ever
    clearing its saved tab list — it stays reopenable) and auto-advances to
    the next pending Group waiting under the same Project.
  </p>
  <p>
    Deleting a Group is a soft delete: it sits in Trash for a retention
    window before it's gone for good, so an accidental delete isn't final.
  </p>

  <h2>Status</h2>
  <table class="status-table">
